%% Platform-admin authentication and control-plane authorization
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Operator as Platform admin
    participant Web as Platform admin web
    participant API as Platform API
    participant Auth as PlatformAuthService
    participant DB as Control-plane PostgreSQL
    participant Guard as PlatformAuthGuard
    participant Service as Platform service

    Operator->>Web: Submit platform credentials
    Web->>API: POST /platform/auth/login
    API->>Auth: Validate login DTO and rate limit
    Auth->>DB: Load PlatformUser
    DB-->>Auth: User, role, permission state
    Auth->>Auth: Verify password and issue platform-realm JWT
    Auth-->>Web: Access token and session response

    Operator->>Web: Open protected platform operation
    Web->>API: GET/POST /platform/* with platform token
    API->>Guard: Validate signature, realm, expiry, role, permissions
    alt Authorized
        Guard->>Service: Continue control-plane operation
        Service->>DB: Read or mutate platform metadata
        DB-->>Service: Control-plane result
        Service-->>Web: Sanitized result
    else Invalid realm or permission
        Guard-->>Web: Stable authorization error
    end

    Note over Auth,DB: Platform auth never resolves a tenant database for ordinary platform operations.
    Note over Guard,Service: Organization IDs in platform routes are operator targets, not browser-selected tenant context.
